    <paragraph>Use the Discriminant to Predict the Number of Solutions of a Quadratic Equation</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, determine the number of solutions to each quadratic equation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="131" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ $$4x^{2} - 5x + 16 = 0$$</item>
          <item>ⓑ $$36y^{2} + 36y + 9 = 0$$</item>
          <item>ⓒ $$6m^{2} + 3m - 5 = 0$$</item>
          <item>ⓓ $$18n^{2} - 7n + 3 = 0$$</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ no real solutions ⓑ 1ⓒ 2 ⓓ no real solutions</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
